+---
+
+# Fix free shipping threshold and quantities
+
+Customers are being charged shipping on orders that should ship free. The rule is: an order whose items come to
+50.00 € or more ships free, quantities included.
+
+## What the request asks
+
+- An order whose items come to exactly 50.00 € (5000 cents) ships free. Today it is charged 4.90 €.
+- An order reaches 50.00 € only once quantities count (for example, three bottles of oil at 17.00 €, 51.00 €) ships
+  free. Today it is charged 4.90 € because shipping adds up unit prices and ignores quantities.
+- Orders below 50.00 € keep the flat 4.90 € shipping charge.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `shippingFor` treats items of 50.00 € or more as free shipping, counting each line's unit price times its quantity.
+- Tests cover: items of exactly 50.00 € ship free; a quantity that takes the items to 50.00 € or more ships free; items
+  of 49.99 € are still charged shipping.
+- The whole test suite passes (`npm test`).
+
+## Decisions taken while building
+
+- The threshold is inclusive (`>=`), as the rule says "50.00 € or more".
+- The fix is in `src/domain/shipping.ts`; `FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS` keeps its value of 5000.
+- Not released: the version in `package.json` and `CHANGELOG.md` are unchanged until the approver approves this change
+  (directive p1).
+
+## Result
+
+- `shippingFor` in `src/domain/shipping.ts` now sums each line's unit price times its quantity, and waives shipping at
+  50.00 € or more (`>=`, was `>`, and it ignored quantities).
+- Tests in `test/shop.test.ts` (`order book`) were written first: the exactly-50.00 € case and the quantity case failed
+  (charged 4.90 €), the 49.99 € case passed. After the fix all 24 tests pass (`npm test`).
+- Not released: `package.json` (1.5.0) and `CHANGELOG.md` are unchanged until the approver approves this change (directive p1).
diff --git a/src/domain/shipping.ts b/src/domain/shipping.ts
index 5c8587fb45c4e5067317ac7db327b8d47df73cd3..9cc75cd8e3bbca46cda3e38ff2f7cefcaa427709 100644
--- a/src/domain/shipping.ts
+++ b/src/domain/shipping.ts
@@ -13,11 +13,11 @@ export interface PricedLine {
 }
 
 /**
- * The shipping charge of an order with these lines.
+ * The shipping charge of an order with these lines. Its items count quantities: a line is its unit price times how many.
  *
  * @param lines - the order's lines, priced
  */
 export function shippingFor(lines: readonly PricedLine[]): Cents {
-  const value = lines.reduce((sum, line) => sum + line.unitPriceCents, 0);
-  return value > FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS ? 0 : SHIPPING_CENTS;
+  const value = lines.reduce((sum, line) => sum + line.unitPriceCents * line.quantity, 0);
+  return value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS ? 0 : SHIPPING_CENTS;
 }
